{{page>meta:infobox:construction&noheader&nofooter&noeditbtn}}

The AP1300 (Cirrus) is a wireless access point with two Ethernet ports. The WAN port has 802.1af PoE, and there are addons for bluetooth or cellphone radios. It ships with [[releases:15.05:start|Chaos Calmer [15.05]]], and is designed exclusively for OpenWrt. It comes with two versions, GL-AP1300LTE is a 4G LTE router with a CAT4 or CAT6 modem, and GL-AP1300 is the standard version. Both of them have built-in PoE and watchdog features.

